/-
# Cassels, Chapter 6, §11: the Witt group of the rationals, Theorem 11.1

Source: J. W. S. Cassels, *Rational Quadratic Forms* (1978), Chapter 6, §11 "The Witt group", pp. 93-96, with the
presentation of $W(k)$ from Chapter 2, Lemma 5.6 and Corollary (pp. 26-27).

**Statement formalized (Theorem 11.1, p. 94).** For every place $p \le \infty$ of $\mathbb Q$ Cassels defines a group
$W(p)$ and a homomorphism $\psi(p) : W(\mathbb Q) \to W(p)$ on the generators $\langle a\rangle$:
* $p = \infty$: $W(\infty) = \mathbb Z$ ($= W(\mathbb R)$), $\psi(\infty)\langle a\rangle = \operatorname{sign}(a)$ (11.8, 11.9);
* $p = 2$: $W(2) = \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z$, $\psi(2)\langle a\rangle = l \bmod 2$ (11.5-11.7);
* $p$ odd: $W(p) = W(\mathbb F_p)$, and for $a = p^{l}u$ with $u$ a $p$-adic unit,
  $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle = \langle\bar u\rangle$ for $l$ odd and $0$ for $l$ even (11.1-11.4).

Theorem 11.1: the maps $\psi(p)$, $p \le \infty$, give an isomorphism of $W(\mathbb Q)$ with the direct sum of the
$W(p)$.

**Formalization.**
* $W(k)$ = `W k` (`Ch2/WittGroup.lean`); $\langle a\rangle$ = `gW a` (`Ch2/WittRing.lean`); $W(k)$ is given by the
  generators $\langle a\rangle$ and relations (i), (ii), (iii) (`W_lift`, Ch. 2, Lemma 5.6 Corollary, in
  `Ch2/WittPresentation.lean`); every homomorphism out of $W(\mathbb Q)$ below is defined through this presentation,
  so its well-definedness is the check of the three relations.
* $\psi(\infty)$ = `psiInf` (relations by the eight sign patterns), $\psi(2)$ = `psiTwo`, and for an odd prime $p$,
  $\psi(p)$ = `psiOdd p`, defined as the odd-valuation component of Cassels' map $\Psi$ for $\mathbb Q_p$
  (`Ch4/Witt.lean`, Lemma 3.1) composed with $\mathbb Q^{\times} \to \mathbb Q_p^{\times}$; this is exactly Cassels'
  "composition of $\psi_p$ with the localization map". `psiOdd_gen` is (11.4).
* The direct sum $\bigoplus_p W(p)$ is written as $\mathbb Z \times \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z \times
  \bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(\mathbb F_p)$ (the summands $W(\infty)$, $W(2)$ separated from the odd primes, so
  that no $W(\mathbb F_2)$ is needed): `Phi : W ℚ →+ ℤ × ZMod 2 × Π₀ p : OddPrime, Wp p`. The odd part is a finitely
  supported family (`DFinsupp`); that $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle = 0$ for all but finitely many $p$ is
  `psiOddAt_gW_of_not_mem`.

**Confirmed from the page image.** The machine-read text of (11.7) is illegible; the page image (p. 93) shows
(11.7) as $\lvert a\rvert_2 = 2^{-l}$, i.e. $l = v_2(a)$, as reconstructed here. We take $\psi(2)\langle a\rangle = v_2(a) \bmod 2$
(the parity of the exponent $l$ in $a = 2^{l}u$, $u$ a $2$-adic unit), the analogue of (11.3)-(11.4) for $p = 2$. This is
consistent with the proof printed on p. 94: $\psi(2)\langle \pm 1\rangle = 0$, $\psi(2)\langle 2\rangle = 1$, and the
relation $\langle 2\rangle + \langle 2\rangle = \langle 1\rangle + \langle 1\rangle$ shows that the kernel of $\psi(2)$
on $L(2)$ is $L'(2)$. The printed remark that $\psi(2)$ "clearly respects the relations" holds for this map by
$v_2(ab(a+b)) = v_2(a) + v_2(b) + v_2(a+b)$. The page images were not readable on the machine where this was written.

**Proof (Cassels, pp. 94-96).** $L(N)$ is the subgroup of $W(\mathbb Q)$ generated by the $\langle n\rangle$ with $n$ a
nonzero integer all of whose prime factors are $\le N$ (`Lsub N`; $L'(p) = L(p-1)$). The union of the $L(N)$ is
$W(\mathbb Q)$ (`exists_Lsub`). By induction on $N$ (`main_ind`) $\Phi$ maps $L(N)$ bijectively onto the tuples that
vanish at all primes $> N$, using for each prime $p$: $\psi(p)$ maps $L(p)$ onto $W(p)$ (`psiOdd_surj`,
`psiTwo_surj`) and the kernel of $\psi(p)$ on $L(p)$ is $L'(p)$ (`ker_psiOdd`, `ker_psiTwo`). For odd $p$ the kernel
statement is proved with Cassels' map $\nu : W(\mathbb F_p) \to L(p)/L'(p)$, $\langle\alpha\rangle \mapsto
\langle p\tilde\alpha\rangle$ (`nu`), well defined by (11.10) (`tilde`).
*Update (proof detail).* In the induction proving (11.10), Cassels multiplies by an element $q$ of $P'(p)$ that
may exceed $p/2$; here this is done with the endomorphism "multiplication by $\langle q\rangle$" of $W(\mathbb Q)$
(`mulQ`), after which the direct step (11.12) (`diffD`) applies; the printed induction is terse at this point.

**Corollaries.** Corollary 1 (kernel of all localizations) is in `Ch6/Sec11.lean` (`localize_injective_everywhere`);
here it is not re-derived.
-/
import QuadFormsKB.Literature.Cassels.Ch4.Witt

open QuadraticMap

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

namespace QuadFormsKB.Cassels.Ch6

open QuadFormsKB.Cassels

local instance instInvertibleTwoRat : Invertible (2 : ℚ) := invertibleOfNonzero two_ne_zero

/-! ### Relations transported along a ring homomorphism -/

section Transport

variable {F K : Type*} [Field F] [Field K] {H : Type*} [AddCommGroup H]

/-- Helper: a function on units of `K` satisfying the relations pulls back along a ring homomorphism. -/
theorem pull_rel1 (φ : F →+* K) (G : Kˣ → H) (h₁ : ∀ a b : Kˣ, G (a * b ^ 2) = G a) :
    ∀ a b : Fˣ, (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) (a * b ^ 2) =
      (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) a := by
  intro a b
  simp only [map_mul, map_pow]
  exact h₁ _ _

/-- Helper: relation (ii) pulls back along a ring homomorphism `φ : F →+* K` (with `G` on the units of `K` satisfying (ii)). -/
theorem pull_rel2 (φ : F →+* K) (G : Kˣ → H)
    (h₂ : ∀ (a b : Kˣ) (hab : (a : K) + b ≠ 0),
      G a + G b = G (Units.mk0 _ hab) + G (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab)) :
    ∀ (a b : Fˣ) (hab : (a : F) + b ≠ 0),
      (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) a + (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) b =
      (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) (Units.mk0 _ hab) +
        (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab) := by
  intro a b hab
  have hab' : ((Units.map φ.toMonoidHom a : Kˣ) : K) + (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom b : Kˣ) ≠ 0 := by
    have : ((Units.map φ.toMonoidHom a : Kˣ) : K) + (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom b : Kˣ) = φ ((a : F) + b) := by
      simp
    rw [this]
    exact fun h => hab (φ.injective (by rw [h, map_zero]))
  have e : Units.map φ.toMonoidHom (Units.mk0 _ hab) = Units.mk0 _ hab' := Units.ext (by simp)
  show G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom a) + G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom b) =
    G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom (Units.mk0 _ hab)) + G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab))
  rw [map_mul, map_mul, e]
  exact h₂ _ _ hab'

/-- Helper: relation (iii), $G(1) + G(-1) = 0$, pulls back along a ring homomorphism `φ : F →+* K`. -/
theorem pull_rel3 (φ : F →+* K) (G : Kˣ → H) (h₃ : G 1 + G (-1) = 0) :
    (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) 1 + (fun x : Fˣ => G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom x)) (-1) = 0 := by
  have e : Units.map φ.toMonoidHom (-1 : Fˣ) = -1 := Units.ext (by simp)
  show G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom 1) + G (Units.map φ.toMonoidHom (-1)) = 0
  rw [map_one, e]
  exact h₃

end Transport

/-! ### The units of ℚ as units of ℚ_p -/

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]

/-- Helper: a rational unit viewed in the units of $\mathbb Q_p$. -/
def castU : ℚˣ →* ℚ_[p]ˣ := Units.map (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]).toMonoidHom

/-- Helper: the underlying element of `castU p a` is the rational $a$ viewed in $\mathbb Q_p$. -/
theorem coe_castU (a : ℚˣ) : ((castU p a : ℚ_[p]ˣ) : ℚ_[p]) = ((a : ℚ) : ℚ_[p]) := rfl

/-- Helper: the map $W(\mathbb Q) \to H$ with $\langle a\rangle \mapsto G(a)$ from a relation-respecting function on
the units of $\mathbb Q_p$. -/
def liftQ {H : Type*} [AddCommGroup H] (G : ℚ_[p]ˣ → H)
    (h₁ : ∀ a b : ℚ_[p]ˣ, G (a * b ^ 2) = G a)
    (h₂ : ∀ (a b : ℚ_[p]ˣ) (hab : (a : ℚ_[p]) + b ≠ 0),
      G a + G b = G (Units.mk0 _ hab) + G (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab))
    (h₃ : G 1 + G (-1) = 0) : W ℚ →+ H :=
  (W_lift (K := ℚ) (fun x : ℚˣ => G (Units.map (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]).toMonoidHom x))
    (pull_rel1 (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]) G h₁) (pull_rel2 (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]) G h₂)
    (pull_rel3 (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]) G h₃)).exists.choose

/-- Helper: `liftQ p G` sends $\langle a\rangle$ to $G(a)$, for $a \in \mathbb Q^{\times}$ viewed in $\mathbb Q_p^{\times}$. -/
theorem liftQ_gen {H : Type*} [AddCommGroup H] (G : ℚ_[p]ˣ → H) (h₁ h₂ h₃) (a : ℚˣ) :
    liftQ p G h₁ h₂ h₃ (gW a) = G (castU p a) :=
  (W_lift (K := ℚ) (fun x : ℚˣ => G (Units.map (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]).toMonoidHom x))
    (pull_rel1 (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]) G h₁) (pull_rel2 (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]) G h₂)
    (pull_rel3 (Rat.castHom ℚ_[p]) G h₃)).exists.choose_spec a

/-! ### The three kinds of maps -/

/-- **Cassels' $\psi(2) : W(\mathbb Q) \to W(2) = \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z$** (Ch. 6, §11, (11.5)-(11.7), p. 93): the
homomorphism with $\psi(2)\langle a\rangle = l \bmod 2$, where $a = 2^{l}u$ with $u$ a $2$-adic unit, i.e. the parity
of the $2$-adic valuation of $a$ (confirmed from the page image, see the module docstring). Defined through the presentation of
$W(\mathbb Q)$ by generators and relations (`W_lift`); the relations (i), (ii), (iii) hold because
$v_2(ab^{2}) \equiv v_2(a)$ and $v_2(ab(a+b)) = v_2(a) + v_2(b) + v_2(a+b)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, (11.5)-(11.7), p. 93 (the map ψ(2))"]
def psiTwo : W ℚ →+ ZMod 2 :=
  liftQ 2 (fun x => ((val 2 x : ℤ) : ZMod 2))
    (fun a b => by
      simp only [_root_.sq]
      rw [(val_mul 2 _ _).1, (val_mul 2 _ _).1]
      push_cast
      have : ((val 2 b : ℤ) : ZMod 2) + (val 2 b : ℤ) = 0 := CharTwo.add_self_eq_zero _
      linear_combination this)
    (fun a b hab => by
      set c := Units.mk0 _ hab
      rw [val_mul3]
      push_cast
      have : ((val 2 c : ℤ) : ZMod 2) + (val 2 c : ℤ) = 0 := CharTwo.add_self_eq_zero _
      linear_combination -this)
    (by
      have h : (-1 : ℚ_[2]).valuation = 0 := by
        have := Padic.valuation_intCast (p := 2) (-1)
        simpa [padicValInt] using this
      simp [val, h])

/-- Helper: $\psi(2)\langle a\rangle$ is the $2$-adic valuation of $a$ modulo $2$. -/
theorem psiTwo_gen (a : ℚˣ) : psiTwo (gW a) = ((val 2 (castU 2 a) : ℤ) : ZMod 2) :=
  liftQ_gen 2 _ _ _ _ a

section Odd

variable [Invertible (2 : ZMod p)]

/-- **Cassels' $\psi(p) : W(\mathbb Q) \to W(p) = W(\mathbb F_p)$ for an odd prime $p$** (Ch. 6, §11, (11.2)-(11.4),
p. 93): the composition of the localization $W(\mathbb Q) \to W(\mathbb Q_p)$ with the second residue map
$W(\mathbb Q_p) \to W(\mathbb F_p)$ of Ch. 3, §3 (here: the odd-valuation component of the isomorphism $\Psi$ of
`witt_padic_odd`, Ch. 4, Lemma 3.1), given on generators by $\langle p^{l}u\rangle \mapsto \langle\bar u\rangle$ for
$l$ odd and $0$ for $l$ even (`psiOdd_gen`). Arguments: `p` a prime (`Fact p.Prime`), with $2$ invertible modulo `p`
(i.e. $p$ odd). -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, (11.2)-(11.4), p. 93 (the maps ψ(p), p odd)"]
def psiOdd : W ℚ →+ W (ZMod p) :=
  liftQ p (fun x => (gψ p x).2)
    (fun a b => by simpa using congrArg Prod.snd (gψ_rel1 p a b))
    (fun a b hab => by simpa using congrArg Prod.snd (gψ_rel2 p a b hab))
    (by simpa using congrArg Prod.snd (gψ_rel3 p))

/-- Helper: $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle = 0$ if $v_p(a)$ is even and $\langle \bar u\rangle$ if odd, where $a = p^{v_p(a)}u$ with $u$ a $p$-adic unit of residue $\bar u$ (Cassels (11.4)). -/
theorem psiOdd_gen (a : ℚˣ) :
    psiOdd p (gW a) = if Even (val p (castU p a)) then 0 else gW (rc p (castU p a)) := by
  rw [psiOdd, liftQ_gen]
  by_cases h : Even (val p (castU p a)) <;> simp [gψ, slot, h]

/-- Helper: the $p$-adic valuation of a rational unit $a$ viewed in $\mathbb Q_p$ is `padicValRat p a`. -/
theorem val_castU (a : ℚˣ) : val p (castU p a) = padicValRat p (a : ℚ) := by
  simp [val, castU]

/-- Helper: $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle = 0$ when the $p$-adic valuation of $a$ is even. -/
theorem psiOdd_gen_of_even (a : ℚˣ) (h : Even (padicValRat p (a : ℚ))) : psiOdd p (gW a) = 0 := by
  rw [psiOdd_gen, if_pos]
  rwa [val_castU]

end Odd

section Integers

/-- Helper: the class $\langle n\rangle \in W(\mathbb Q)$ of a nonzero integer $n$, and $0$ for $n = 0$. -/
def gI (n : ℤ) : W ℚ := if h : n ≠ 0 then gW (Units.mk0 (n : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr h)) else 0

/-- Helper: for $n \ne 0$, `gI n` is the class $\langle n\rangle$ of the rational unit $n$. -/
theorem gI_eq {n : ℤ} (h : n ≠ 0) : gI n = gW (Units.mk0 (n : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr h)) := dif_pos h

/-- Helper: `gI 0 = 0`. -/
theorem gI_zero : gI 0 = 0 := dif_neg (by simp)

/-- Helper: relation (i) for integers: $\langle n m^{2}\rangle = \langle n\rangle$ for $m \ne 0$. -/
theorem gI_sq (n : ℤ) {m : ℤ} (hm : m ≠ 0) : gI (n * m ^ 2) = gI n := by
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn; simp [gI_zero]
  · have hnm : n * m ^ 2 ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero hn (pow_ne_zero 2 hm)
    rw [gI_eq hnm, gI_eq hn, ← gW_sq (Units.mk0 (n : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hn))
      (Units.mk0 (m : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hm))]
    congr 1
    exact Units.ext (by simp)

/-- Helper: $\langle -n\rangle = -\langle n\rangle$ in $W(\mathbb Q)$ (from $\langle n\rangle + \langle -n\rangle = 0$). -/
theorem gI_neg (n : ℤ) : gI (-n) = -gI n := by
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn; simp [gI_zero]
  · rw [gI_eq (neg_ne_zero.mpr hn), gI_eq hn]
    have e : Units.mk0 (((-n : ℤ)) : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr (neg_ne_zero.mpr hn)) =
        -Units.mk0 (n : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hn) := Units.ext (by simp)
    rw [e]
    exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_right (gW_add_neg _)

/-- Helper: relation (ii) for integers: $\langle n\rangle + \langle m\rangle = \langle n+m\rangle + \langle nm(n+m)\rangle$ when $n, m, n+m \ne 0$. -/
theorem gI_add {n m : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ 0) (hm : m ≠ 0) (hnm : n + m ≠ 0) :
    gI n + gI m = gI (n + m) + gI (n * m * (n + m)) := by
  have hprod : n * m * (n + m) ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero hn hm) hnm
  have hq : ((Units.mk0 (n : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hn) : ℚˣ) : ℚ) +
      (Units.mk0 (m : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hm) : ℚˣ) ≠ 0 := by
    simpa using (Int.cast_ne_zero (α := ℚ)).mpr hnm
  rw [gI_eq hn, gI_eq hm, gI_eq hnm, gI_eq hprod, gW_add _ _ hq]
  congr 2
  · exact Units.ext (by simp)
  · exact Units.ext (by simp)

end Integers

/-! ### Signature -/

/-- Helper: the sign $\pm 1$ of a nonzero rational. -/
def sgn (x : ℚˣ) : ℤ := if 0 < (x : ℚ) then 1 else -1

/-- Helper: relation (i) for the sign: $\operatorname{sign}(ab^{2}) = \operatorname{sign}(a)$. -/
theorem sgn_rel1 (a b : ℚˣ) : sgn (a * b ^ 2) = sgn a := by
  have hb : (0 : ℚ) < (b : ℚ) ^ 2 := by have := b.ne_zero; positivity
  unfold sgn
  simp only [Units.val_mul, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val]
  by_cases ha : 0 < (a : ℚ)
  · rw [if_pos ha, if_pos (mul_pos ha hb)]
  · rw [if_neg ha, if_neg (fun h => ha ((mul_pos_iff_of_pos_right hb).mp h))]

/-- Helper: relation (ii) for the sign, by the eight sign patterns of $a$, $b$, $a+b$. -/
theorem sgn_rel2 (a b : ℚˣ) (hab : (a : ℚ) + b ≠ 0) :
    sgn a + sgn b = sgn (Units.mk0 _ hab) + sgn (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab) := by
  unfold sgn
  simp only [Units.val_mul, Units.val_mk0]
  have ha := a.ne_zero
  have hb := b.ne_zero
  rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne ha with ha' | ha' <;> rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hb with hb' | hb'
  · have h1 : (a : ℚ) + b < 0 := by linarith
    have h2 : (a : ℚ) * b * (a + b) < 0 := by nlinarith [mul_pos_of_neg_of_neg ha' hb']
    simp [not_lt.mpr ha'.le, not_lt.mpr hb'.le, not_lt.mpr h1.le, not_lt.mpr h2.le]
  · rcases lt_trichotomy ((a : ℚ) + b) 0 with h1 | h1 | h1
    · have h2 : 0 < (a : ℚ) * b * (a + b) := by nlinarith [mul_neg_of_neg_of_pos ha' hb']
      simp [not_lt.mpr ha'.le, hb', not_lt.mpr h1.le, h2]
    · exact absurd h1 hab
    · have h2 : (a : ℚ) * b * (a + b) < 0 := by nlinarith [mul_neg_of_neg_of_pos ha' hb']
      simp [not_lt.mpr ha'.le, hb', h1, not_lt.mpr h2.le]
  · rcases lt_trichotomy ((a : ℚ) + b) 0 with h1 | h1 | h1
    · have h2 : 0 < (a : ℚ) * b * (a + b) := by nlinarith [mul_neg_of_pos_of_neg ha' hb']
      simp [ha', not_lt.mpr hb'.le, not_lt.mpr h1.le, h2]
    · exact absurd h1 hab
    · have h2 : (a : ℚ) * b * (a + b) < 0 := by nlinarith [mul_neg_of_pos_of_neg ha' hb']
      simp [ha', not_lt.mpr hb'.le, h1, not_lt.mpr h2.le]
  · have h1 : 0 < (a : ℚ) + b := by linarith
    have h2 : 0 < (a : ℚ) * b * (a + b) := by positivity
    simp [ha', hb', h1, h2]

/-- Helper: relation (iii) for the sign: $\operatorname{sign}(1) + \operatorname{sign}(-1) = 0$. -/
theorem sgn_rel3 : sgn 1 + sgn (-1) = 0 := by
  unfold sgn; norm_num

/-- **Cassels' $\psi(\infty) : W(\mathbb Q) \to W(\infty) = \mathbb Z$** (Ch. 6, §11, (11.8)-(11.9), p. 94): the
homomorphism with $\psi(\infty)\langle a\rangle = +1$ for $a > 0$ and $-1$ for $a < 0$ (the signature; $W(\infty) = W(\mathbb R)
\cong \mathbb Z$ by Ch. 2, Lemma 5.7 Corollary). Defined through the presentation of $W(\mathbb Q)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, (11.8)-(11.9), p. 94 (the map ψ(∞))"]
def psiInf : W ℚ →+ ℤ := (W_lift (K := ℚ) sgn sgn_rel1 sgn_rel2 sgn_rel3).exists.choose

/-- Cassels (11.9): $\psi(\infty)\langle a\rangle = \operatorname{sign}(a) = \pm 1$. -/
theorem psiInf_gen (a : ℚˣ) : psiInf (gW a) = sgn a :=
  (W_lift (K := ℚ) sgn sgn_rel1 sgn_rel2 sgn_rel3).exists.choose_spec a

/-! ### Values on integers -/

theorem psiInf_gI {n : ℤ} (h : n ≠ 0) : psiInf (gI n) = if 0 < n then 1 else -1 := by
  rw [gI_eq h, psiInf_gen]
  simp [sgn]

/-- Helper: $\psi(2)\langle n\rangle = v_2(n) \bmod 2$ for a nonzero integer $n$. -/
theorem psiTwo_gI {n : ℤ} (h : n ≠ 0) : psiTwo (gI n) = ((padicValInt 2 n : ℕ) : ZMod 2) := by
  rw [gI_eq h, psiTwo_gen]
  have : val 2 (castU 2 (Units.mk0 (n : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr h))) = (padicValInt 2 n : ℕ) := by
    simp [val, castU]
  rw [this]
  simp

section OddInt

variable [Invertible (2 : ZMod p)]

/-- Helper: for $m$ prime to $p$ and $n = p^{k}m$, the $p$-adic valuation of $n$ is $k$ and the residue of its unit part is $m \bmod p$. -/
theorem val_rc_int (m : ℤ) (hm : ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ m) (k : ℕ) (hn : (p : ℤ) ^ k * m ≠ 0) :
    val p (castU p (Units.mk0 (((p : ℤ) ^ k * m : ℤ) : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hn))) = k ∧
    ((rc p (castU p (Units.mk0 (((p : ℤ) ^ k * m : ℤ) : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hn))) : (ZMod p)ˣ) :
      ZMod p) = (m : ZMod p) := by
  have hu : IsUnit (m : ℤ_[p]) := isUnit_of_toZMod_ne_zero p (by
    rw [map_intCast]
    exact fun h => hm ((ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd m p).mp h))
  obtain ⟨hv, hw⟩ := decomp_unique p (x := castU p (Units.mk0 (((p : ℤ) ^ k * m : ℤ) : ℚ)
      (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hn))) (l := k) (w := hu.unit) (by
    rw [coe_castU, IsUnit.unit_spec]
    simp [PadicInt.coe_intCast, zpow_natCast])
  refine ⟨hv, ?_⟩
  rw [rc, hw, coe_unitF, IsUnit.unit_spec, map_intCast]

/-- Helper: $\psi(p)\langle n\rangle = 0$ for an integer $n$ prime to $p$. -/
theorem psiOdd_gI_of_not_dvd {n : ℤ} (hp : ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ n) : psiOdd p (gI n) = 0 := by
  have hn : n ≠ 0 := fun h => hp (h ▸ dvd_zero _)
  have hn' : (p : ℤ) ^ 0 * n ≠ 0 := by simpa using hn
  rw [gI_eq hn, psiOdd_gen, if_pos]
  have := (val_rc_int p n hp 0 hn').1
  simp only [pow_zero, one_mul] at this
  rw [this]
  simp

/-- Helper: $\psi(p)\langle pm\rangle = \langle \bar m\rangle$ for an integer $m$ prime to $p$. -/
theorem psiOdd_gI_prime_mul {m : ℤ} (hm : ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ m) :
    psiOdd p (gI ((p : ℤ) * m)) = gW (Units.mk0 (m : ZMod p) (fun h =>
      hm ((ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd m p).mp h))) := by
  have hm0 : m ≠ 0 := fun h => hm (h ▸ dvd_zero _)
  have hpm : (p : ℤ) * m ≠ 0 :=
    mul_ne_zero (by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero) hm0
  have hn' : (p : ℤ) ^ 1 * m ≠ 0 := by simpa using hpm
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := val_rc_int p m hm 1 hn'
  rw [gI_eq hpm, psiOdd_gen]
  simp only [pow_one] at h1 h2
  rw [if_neg]
  · congr 1
    exact Units.ext h2
  · rw [h1]
    simp

end OddInt

/-! ### The filtration of $W(\mathbb Q)$ by the prime factors -/

/-- Helper: $n$ is a nonzero integer all of whose prime factors are at most $N$. -/
def PInt (N : ℕ) (n : ℤ) : Prop := n ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → (q : ℤ) ∣ n → q ≤ N

/-- Helper: elements of $P(N)$ are nonzero. -/
theorem PInt.ne_zero {N : ℕ} {n : ℤ} (h : PInt N n) : n ≠ 0 := h.1

/-- Helper: $P(N) \subseteq P(M)$ for $N \le M$. -/
theorem PInt.mono {N M : ℕ} (hNM : N ≤ M) {n : ℤ} (h : PInt N n) : PInt M n :=
  ⟨h.1, fun q hq hd => (h.2 q hq hd).trans hNM⟩

/-- Helper: $P(N)$ is closed under products. -/
theorem PInt.mul {N : ℕ} {a b : ℤ} (ha : PInt N a) (hb : PInt N b) : PInt N (a * b) :=
  ⟨mul_ne_zero ha.1 hb.1, fun q hq hd => by
    rcases Int.Prime.dvd_mul' hq hd with h | h
    · exact ha.2 q hq h
    · exact hb.2 q hq h⟩

/-- Helper: $P(N)$ is closed under negation. -/
theorem PInt.neg {N : ℕ} {a : ℤ} (ha : PInt N a) : PInt N (-a) :=
  ⟨neg_ne_zero.mpr ha.1, fun q hq hd => ha.2 q hq ((dvd_neg).mp hd)⟩

/-- Helper: a nonzero divisor `b` of an element `a` of $P(N)$ lies in $P(N)$. -/
theorem PInt.of_dvd {N : ℕ} {a b : ℤ} (hb : b ≠ 0) (hab : b ∣ a) (ha : PInt N a) : PInt N b :=
  ⟨hb, fun q hq hd => ha.2 q hq (hd.trans hab)⟩

/-- Helper: $1 \in P(N)$. -/
theorem PInt.one (N : ℕ) : PInt N 1 :=
  ⟨one_ne_zero, fun q hq hd => absurd (Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp (by simpa using hd) : q ∣ 1) hq.not_dvd_one⟩

/-- Helper: a nonzero integer of absolute value at most $N$ lies in $P(N)$. -/
theorem PInt.of_natAbs_le {N : ℕ} {n : ℤ} (h0 : n ≠ 0) (h : n.natAbs ≤ N) : PInt N n :=
  ⟨h0, fun _ _ hd => (Nat.le_of_dvd (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr h0) (Int.natCast_dvd.mp hd)).trans h⟩

/-- Helper: the subgroup $L(N)$ of $W(\mathbb Q)$ generated by the $\langle n\rangle$ with $n$ a nonzero integer
all of whose prime factors are at most $N$. -/
def Lsub (N : ℕ) : AddSubgroup (W ℚ) := AddSubgroup.closure {x | ∃ n : ℤ, PInt N n ∧ x = gI n}

/-- Helper: $\langle n\rangle \in L(N)$ for $n \in P(N)$. -/
theorem gI_mem_Lsub {N : ℕ} {n : ℤ} (h : PInt N n) : gI n ∈ Lsub N :=
  AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨n, h, rfl⟩

/-- Helper: $L(N) \subseteq L(M)$ for $N \le M$. -/
theorem Lsub_mono {N M : ℕ} (h : N ≤ M) : Lsub N ≤ Lsub M := by
  apply AddSubgroup.closure_mono
  rintro x ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨n, hn.mono h, rfl⟩

/-- Helper: multiplication by $\langle q\rangle$ on $W(\mathbb Q)$ for a nonzero integer $q$. -/
def mulQ (q : ℤ) (hq : q ≠ 0) : W ℚ →+ W ℚ := mulByW (Units.mk0 (q : ℚ) (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hq))

/-- Helper: multiplication by $\langle q\rangle$ sends $\langle n\rangle$ to $\langle qn\rangle$. -/
theorem mulQ_gI (q : ℤ) (hq : q ≠ 0) (n : ℤ) : mulQ q hq (gI n) = gI (q * n) := by
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn; simp [gI_zero]
  · rw [gI_eq hn, gI_eq (mul_ne_zero hq hn), mulQ, mulByW_gen]
    congr 1
    exact Units.ext (by simp)

/-- Helper: multiplication by $\langle q\rangle$ with $q \in P(N)$ preserves $L(N)$. -/
theorem mulQ_mem {N : ℕ} {q : ℤ} (hq : PInt N q) {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub N) :
    mulQ q hq.1 x ∈ Lsub N := by
  refine AddSubgroup.closure_induction (p := fun x _ => mulQ q hq.1 x ∈ Lsub N)
    (fun y hy => ?_) ?_ (fun x y _ _ hx hy => ?_) (fun x _ hx => ?_) hx
  · obtain ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩ := hy
    rw [mulQ_gI]
    exact gI_mem_Lsub (hq.mul hn)
  · rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  · rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hx hy
  · rw [map_neg]; exact neg_mem hx

/-- Helper (the congruence step behind Cassels' (11.12)): if $u = v + P t$ with $u, v$ and $t$ (or $t = 0$) in
$P(N)$, then $\langle P u\rangle - \langle P v\rangle \in L(N)$. -/
theorem diffD {N : ℕ} {P : ℤ} (hP : P ≠ 0) {u v t : ℤ} (huv : u = v + P * t) (hu : PInt N u)
    (hv : PInt N v) (ht : t = 0 ∨ PInt N t) : gI (P * u) - gI (P * v) ∈ Lsub N := by
  rcases ht with rfl | ht
  · simp only [mul_zero, add_zero] at huv
    subst huv
    simp
  · have hn : P * v ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero hP hv.1
    have hm : P ^ 2 * t ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero (pow_ne_zero 2 hP) ht.1
    have hsum : P * v + P ^ 2 * t = P * u := by rw [huv]; ring
    have hnm : P * v + P ^ 2 * t ≠ 0 := by rw [hsum]; exact mul_ne_zero hP hu.1
    have key := gI_add hn hm hnm
    rw [hsum] at key
    have e1 : gI (P ^ 2 * t) = gI t := by rw [mul_comm]; exact gI_sq t hP
    have e2 : gI (P * v * (P ^ 2 * t) * (P * u)) = gI (v * t * u) := by
      have : P * v * (P ^ 2 * t) * (P * u) = v * t * u * (P ^ 2) ^ 2 := by ring
      rw [this]; exact gI_sq _ (pow_ne_zero 2 hP)
    rw [e1, e2] at key
    have h' : gI (P * u) - gI (P * v) = gI t - gI (v * t * u) := by
      rw [sub_eq_sub_iff_add_eq_add, add_comm (gI t), ← key, add_comm]
    rw [h']
    exact sub_mem (gI_mem_Lsub ht) (gI_mem_Lsub ((hv.mul ht).mul hu))

section Tilde

variable {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] (hp2 : p ≠ 2)

include hp2 in
/-- Helper: a prime $p \ne 2$ is at least $3$. -/
theorem three_le_of_ne_two : 3 ≤ p := by
  have := (Fact.out : p.Prime).two_le
  omega

include hp2 in
/-- Helper: a prime $p \ne 2$ is odd. -/
theorem p_odd_of_ne_two : Odd p := (Fact.out : p.Prime).odd_of_ne_two hp2

/-- Helper: $c$ lies strictly between $-p/2$ and $p/2$. -/
def Small (p : ℕ) (c : ℤ) : Prop := -(p : ℤ) < 2 * c ∧ 2 * c < p

include hp2 in
/-- Helper: the representative of $\alpha \in \mathbb F_p$ of least absolute value ($p$ odd) is small, $-p/2 < c < p/2$. -/
theorem valMinAbs_small (α : ZMod p) : Small p α.valMinAbs := by
  have hI := ZMod.valMinAbs_mem_Ioc α
  obtain ⟨hlo, hhi⟩ := hI
  have hodd := p_odd_of_ne_two hp2
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hodd
  constructor
  · by_contra h
    have : 2 * α.valMinAbs = -(p : ℤ) := by omega
    omega
  · by_contra h
    have : 2 * α.valMinAbs = (p : ℤ) := by omega
    omega

include hp2 in
/-- Helper: a nonzero small integer has all prime factors less than $p$, i.e. lies in $P'(p) = P(p-1)$. -/
theorem PInt_of_small {c : ℤ} (hc0 : c ≠ 0) (hs : Small p c) : PInt (p - 1) c := by
  refine ⟨hc0, fun q _ hd => ?_⟩
  have h1 : q ≤ c.natAbs := Nat.le_of_dvd (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hc0) (Int.natCast_dvd.mp hd)
  have h2 : 2 * c.natAbs < p := by
    have := hs.1; have := hs.2
    omega
  omega

/-- Helper: an element of $P'(p)$ is prime to $p$. -/
theorem not_dvd_of_PInt {u : ℤ} (h : PInt (p - 1) u) : ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ u := by
  intro hd
  have := h.2 p Fact.out hd
  have := (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos
  omega

/-- Helper: an element of $P'(p)$ is nonzero modulo $p$. -/
theorem cast_ne_zero_of_PInt {u : ℤ} (h : PInt (p - 1) u) : (u : ZMod p) ≠ 0 :=
  fun h0 => not_dvd_of_PInt h ((ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd u p).mp h0)

include hp2 in
/-- Helper: Cassels' (11.10) when $v$ is small: if $u \equiv v \pmod p$, $u \in P'(p)$ and $v$ is small, then
$\langle pu\rangle \equiv \langle pv\rangle \pmod{L'(p)}$ (induction on $|u|$). -/
theorem tilde_aux : ∀ (n : ℕ) (u : ℤ), u.natAbs = n → PInt (p - 1) u → ∀ v : ℤ, Small p v → v ≠ 0 →
    (u : ZMod p) = v → gI (p * u) - gI (p * v) ∈ Lsub (p - 1) := by
  have hp3 := three_le_of_ne_two hp2
  have hp0 : (p : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero
  intro n
  induction n using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | _ n ih =>
  intro u hun hu v hv hv0 huv
  by_cases hs : Small p u
  · have hdvd : (p : ℤ) ∣ v - u := (ZMod.intCast_eq_intCast_iff_dvd_sub u v p).mp huv
    have h0 : v - u = 0 := by
      apply Int.eq_zero_of_abs_lt_dvd hdvd
      rw [abs_lt]
      have := hs.1; have := hs.2; have := hv.1; have := hv.2
      constructor <;> omega
    have : u = v := by omega
    subst this
    simp
  · -- u is not small: u = q * u₁
    have hk : 2 ≤ u.natAbs := by
      by_contra hlt
      have h1 : u.natAbs ≤ 1 := by omega
      apply hs
      have := Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hu.1
      constructor <;> omega
    set q := u.natAbs.minFac with hq
    have hqp : q.Prime := Nat.minFac_prime (by omega)
    have hqdvd : (q : ℤ) ∣ u := Int.natCast_dvd.mpr (Nat.minFac_dvd _)
    obtain ⟨u₁, hu₁⟩ := hqdvd
    have hq1 : 2 ≤ q := hqp.two_le
    have hq0 : (q : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hqp.ne_zero
    have hu₁0 : u₁ ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; exact hu.1 (by simpa using hu₁)
    have hnat : u.natAbs = q * u₁.natAbs := by
      rw [hu₁, Int.natAbs_mul]; simp
    have hlt : u₁.natAbs < n := by
      rw [← hun, hnat]
      have := Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hu₁0
      nlinarith
    have hPu₁ : PInt (p - 1) u₁ := hu.of_dvd hu₁0 ⟨q, by rw [hu₁]; ring⟩
    have hPq : PInt (p - 1) (q : ℤ) := hu.of_dvd hq0 ⟨u₁, hu₁⟩
    have hqle : q ≤ p - 1 := hu.2 q hqp ⟨u₁, hu₁⟩
    set v₁ := (u₁ : ZMod p).valMinAbs with hv₁
    have hv₁s : Small p v₁ := valMinAbs_small hp2 _
    have hv₁0 : v₁ ≠ 0 := by
      rw [hv₁, Ne, ZMod.valMinAbs_eq_zero]
      exact cast_ne_zero_of_PInt hPu₁
    have hv₁c : (u₁ : ZMod p) = v₁ := (ZMod.coe_valMinAbs _).symm
    have IH := ih u₁.natAbs hlt u₁ rfl hPu₁ v₁ hv₁s hv₁0 hv₁c
    have h1 := mulQ_mem hPq IH
    rw [map_sub, mulQ_gI, mulQ_gI] at h1
    -- compare q * v₁ with v
    have hcongr : (v : ZMod p) = (((q : ℤ) * v₁ : ℤ) : ZMod p) := by
      have h3 : (u : ZMod p) = (((q : ℤ) * v₁ : ℤ) : ZMod p) := by
        rw [hu₁, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_mul, hv₁c]
      exact huv.symm.trans h3
    have hdvd : (p : ℤ) ∣ (q : ℤ) * v₁ - v := (ZMod.intCast_eq_intCast_iff_dvd_sub v _ p).mp hcongr
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hdvd
    have hPqv : PInt (p - 1) ((q : ℤ) * v₁) := hPq.mul (PInt_of_small hp2 hv₁0 hv₁s)
    have hPv : PInt (p - 1) v := PInt_of_small hp2 hv0 hv
    have htt : t = 0 ∨ PInt (p - 1) t := by
      by_cases ht0 : t = 0
      · exact Or.inl ht0
      · right
        apply PInt_of_small hp2 ht0
        have hpp : (0 : ℤ) < p := by omega
        have hqle' : (q : ℤ) ≤ p - 1 := by omega
        have a1 := hv₁s.1; have a2 := hv₁s.2; have a3 := hv.1; have a4 := hv.2
        have hq0' : (0 : ℤ) ≤ q := by positivity
        constructor
        · by_contra hcon
          have : 2 * (p : ℤ) * t ≤ -(p : ℤ) * p := by nlinarith
          nlinarith [mul_nonneg hq0' (show (0 : ℤ) ≤ p - 1 - 2 * v₁ by omega),
            mul_nonneg hq0' (show (0 : ℤ) ≤ p - 1 + 2 * v₁ by omega)]
        · by_contra hcon
          have : (p : ℤ) * p ≤ 2 * (p : ℤ) * t := by nlinarith
          nlinarith [mul_nonneg hq0' (show (0 : ℤ) ≤ p - 1 - 2 * v₁ by omega),
            mul_nonneg hq0' (show (0 : ℤ) ≤ p - 1 + 2 * v₁ by omega)]
    have h2 := diffD (N := p - 1) hp0 (u := (q : ℤ) * v₁) (v := v) (t := t) (by linarith) hPqv hPv htt
    have e1 : (p : ℤ) * u = (q : ℤ) * (p * u₁) := by rw [hu₁]; ring
    have e2 : (q : ℤ) * ((p : ℤ) * v₁) = p * ((q : ℤ) * v₁) := by ring
    rw [e2] at h1
    have := add_mem h1 h2
    rw [e1]
    simpa using this

include hp2 in
/-- **Cassels' (11.10)** (Ch. 6, §11, p. 95). If $u, v \in P'(p)$ (nonzero integers all of whose prime factors are
less than $p$) and $u \equiv v \pmod p$, then $\langle pu\rangle \equiv \langle pv\rangle \pmod{L'(p)}$, i.e.
$\langle pu\rangle - \langle pv\rangle \in L(p-1)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, (11.10), p. 95"]
theorem tilde {u v : ℤ} (hu : PInt (p - 1) u) (hv : PInt (p - 1) v) (h : (u : ZMod p) = v) :
    gI (p * u) - gI (p * v) ∈ Lsub (p - 1) := by
  set w := (u : ZMod p).valMinAbs with hw
  have hws : Small p w := valMinAbs_small hp2 _
  have hw0 : w ≠ 0 := by
    rw [hw, Ne, ZMod.valMinAbs_eq_zero]
    exact cast_ne_zero_of_PInt hu
  have hwc : (u : ZMod p) = w := (ZMod.coe_valMinAbs _).symm
  have h1 := tilde_aux hp2 _ u rfl hu w hws hw0 hwc
  have h2 := tilde_aux hp2 _ v rfl hv w hws hw0 (h ▸ hwc).symm.symm
  have := sub_mem h1 h2
  simpa using this

end Tilde

section Nu

variable {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [Invertible (2 : ZMod p)]

/-- Helper: if $2$ is invertible modulo the prime $p$ then $p \ne 2$. -/
theorem p_ne_two_of_inv : p ≠ 2 := by
  rintro rfl
  have h : (2 : ZMod 2) = 0 := by exact_mod_cast CharP.cast_eq_zero (ZMod 2) 2
  exact Invertible.ne_zero (2 : ZMod 2) h

/-- Helper: the values of Cassels' map $\nu$ on generators: $\alpha \mapsto \langle p\tilde\alpha\rangle \bmod L'(p)$,
where $\tilde\alpha$ is the integer representative of $\alpha$ with $-p/2 < \tilde\alpha < p/2$. -/
def nuGen (α : (ZMod p)ˣ) : W ℚ ⧸ Lsub (p - 1) :=
  QuotientAddGroup.mk (gI ((p : ℤ) * (α : ZMod p).valMinAbs))

/-- Helper: $\nu(\alpha) = \langle pm\rangle \bmod L'(p)$ for any $m \in P'(p)$ with $m \equiv \alpha \pmod p$ (Cassels (11.10)). -/
theorem nuGen_eq (α : (ZMod p)ˣ) {m : ℤ} (hm : PInt (p - 1) m) (h : (m : ZMod p) = α) :
    nuGen α = QuotientAddGroup.mk (gI ((p : ℤ) * m)) := by
  have hp2 := p_ne_two_of_inv (p := p)
  have hc0 : (α : ZMod p).valMinAbs ≠ 0 := by
    rw [Ne, ZMod.valMinAbs_eq_zero]; exact α.ne_zero
  have hc : PInt (p - 1) (α : ZMod p).valMinAbs := PInt_of_small hp2 hc0 (valMinAbs_small hp2 _)
  have := tilde hp2 hc hm (by rw [ZMod.coe_valMinAbs, h])
  exact (QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem).mpr this

/-- Helper: the small representative of a unit of $\mathbb F_p$ lies in $P'(p)$. -/
theorem PInt_valMinAbs (α : (ZMod p)ˣ) : PInt (p - 1) (α : ZMod p).valMinAbs := by
  have hp2 := p_ne_two_of_inv (p := p)
  exact PInt_of_small hp2 (by rw [Ne, ZMod.valMinAbs_eq_zero]; exact α.ne_zero) (valMinAbs_small hp2 _)

/-- Helper: relation (i) for $\nu$ on generators. -/
theorem nu_rel1 (a b : (ZMod p)ˣ) : nuGen (a * b ^ 2) = nuGen a := by
  have hc := PInt_valMinAbs a
  have hd := PInt_valMinAbs b
  have hp0 : (p : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero
  rw [nuGen_eq (a * b ^ 2) (m := (a : ZMod p).valMinAbs * ((b : ZMod p).valMinAbs * (b : ZMod p).valMinAbs))
    (hc.mul (hd.mul hd)) (by simp [ZMod.coe_valMinAbs]; ring)]
  have : (p : ℤ) * ((a : ZMod p).valMinAbs * ((b : ZMod p).valMinAbs * (b : ZMod p).valMinAbs)) =
      ((p : ℤ) * (a : ZMod p).valMinAbs) * (b : ZMod p).valMinAbs ^ 2 := by ring
  rw [this, gI_sq _ hd.1]
  rfl

/-- Helper: relation (ii) for $\nu$ on generators (Cassels, p. 96). -/
theorem nu_rel2 (a b : (ZMod p)ˣ) (hab : (a : ZMod p) + b ≠ 0) :
    nuGen a + nuGen b = nuGen (Units.mk0 _ hab) + nuGen (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab) := by
  have hp2 := p_ne_two_of_inv (p := p)
  have hc := PInt_valMinAbs a
  have hd := PInt_valMinAbs b
  set c := (a : ZMod p).valMinAbs with hcdef
  set d := (b : ZMod p).valMinAbs with hddef
  have hcs := valMinAbs_small hp2 (a : ZMod p)
  have hds := valMinAbs_small hp2 (b : ZMod p)
  have hcd0 : c + d ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    apply hab
    have : ((c + d : ℤ) : ZMod p) = 0 := by rw [h]; simp
    simpa [hcdef, hddef, ZMod.coe_valMinAbs] using this
  have hsum : PInt (p - 1) (c + d) := by
    refine PInt.of_natAbs_le hcd0 ?_
    have := hcs.1; have := hcs.2; have := hds.1; have := hds.2
    omega
  have hprod : PInt (p - 1) (c * d * (c + d)) := (hc.mul hd).mul hsum
  have hp0 : (p : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero
  rw [nuGen_eq (Units.mk0 _ hab) hsum (by simp [hcdef, hddef, ZMod.coe_valMinAbs]),
    nuGen_eq (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab) hprod (by simp [hcdef, hddef, ZMod.coe_valMinAbs])]
  have key := gI_add (n := (p : ℤ) * c) (m := (p : ℤ) * d) (mul_ne_zero hp0 hc.1) (mul_ne_zero hp0 hd.1)
    (by rw [← mul_add]; exact mul_ne_zero hp0 hcd0)
  have e1 : (p : ℤ) * c + (p : ℤ) * d = (p : ℤ) * (c + d) := by ring
  have e2 : (p : ℤ) * c * ((p : ℤ) * d) * ((p : ℤ) * (c + d)) =
      ((p : ℤ) * (c * d * (c + d))) * (p : ℤ) ^ 2 := by ring
  rw [e1, e2, gI_sq _ hp0] at key
  show QuotientAddGroup.mk (gI ((p : ℤ) * c)) + QuotientAddGroup.mk (gI ((p : ℤ) * d)) = _
  rw [← QuotientAddGroup.mk_add, key, QuotientAddGroup.mk_add]

/-- Helper: relation (iii) for $\nu$ on generators. -/
theorem nu_rel3 : nuGen (1 : (ZMod p)ˣ) + nuGen (-1 : (ZMod p)ˣ) = 0 := by
  rw [nuGen_eq 1 (m := 1) (PInt.one _) (by simp), nuGen_eq (-1) (m := -1) (PInt.one _).neg (by simp)]
  rw [← QuotientAddGroup.mk_add, mul_one, mul_neg_one, gI_neg, add_neg_cancel]
  rfl

/-- Helper: Cassels' map $\nu : W(\mathbb F_p) \to W(\mathbb Q)/L'(p)$ (Ch. 6, §11, p. 95), through the
presentation of $W(\mathbb F_p)$ (Ch. 2, Lemma 5.6, Corollary). -/
def nu : W (ZMod p) →+ W ℚ ⧸ Lsub (p - 1) :=
  (W_lift (K := ZMod p) nuGen nu_rel1 nu_rel2 nu_rel3).exists.choose

/-- Helper: $\nu\langle\alpha\rangle = \langle p\tilde\alpha\rangle \bmod L'(p)$. -/
theorem nu_gen (α : (ZMod p)ˣ) : nu (gW α) = nuGen α :=
  (W_lift (K := ZMod p) nuGen nu_rel1 nu_rel2 nu_rel3).exists.choose_spec α

end Nu

/-- Helper: every nonzero integer is $p^{k} m$ with $p \nmid m$. -/
theorem exists_pow_mul (p : ℕ) (hp : 2 ≤ p) :
    ∀ (N : ℕ) (n : ℤ), n.natAbs = N → n ≠ 0 → ∃ (k : ℕ) (m : ℤ), ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ m ∧ n = (p : ℤ) ^ k * m := by
  intro N
  induction N using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | _ N ih =>
  intro n hn hn0
  by_cases h : (p : ℤ) ∣ n
  · obtain ⟨n', rfl⟩ := h
    have hn'0 : n' ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; simp at hn0
    have hlt : n'.natAbs < N := by
      rw [← hn, Int.natAbs_mul]
      have := Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hn'0
      simp only [Int.natAbs_natCast]
      nlinarith
    obtain ⟨k, m, hm, he⟩ := ih n'.natAbs hlt n' rfl hn'0
    exact ⟨k + 1, m, hm, by rw [he]; ring⟩
  · exact ⟨0, n, h, by simp⟩

section Local

variable {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [Invertible (2 : ZMod p)]

/-- Helper: if $n = p^{k}m \in P(p)$ with $p \nmid m$ then $m \in P'(p)$. -/
theorem PInt_cofactor {n m : ℤ} {k : ℕ} (hn : PInt p n) (hm : ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ m) (he : n = (p : ℤ) ^ k * m) :
    PInt (p - 1) m := by
  have hm0 : m ≠ 0 := fun h => hm (h ▸ dvd_zero _)
  refine ⟨hm0, fun q hq hd => ?_⟩
  have h1 : q ≤ p := hn.2 q hq (hd.trans ⟨(p : ℤ) ^ k, by rw [he]; ring⟩)
  rcases Nat.lt_or_ge q p with h | h
  · omega
  · exfalso
    have : q = p := by omega
    subst this
    exact hm hd

/-- Helper: $\nu \circ \psi(p)$ agrees with the quotient map on the generators of $L(p)$. -/
theorem theta_gen {n : ℤ} (hn : PInt p n) :
    (nu (p := p)) (psiOdd p (gI n)) = QuotientAddGroup.mk (gI n) := by
  have hp0 : (p : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero
  obtain ⟨k, m, hm, he⟩ := exists_pow_mul p (Fact.out : p.Prime).two_le _ n rfl hn.1
  have hPm := PInt_cofactor hn hm he
  obtain ⟨j, hj | hj⟩ := Nat.even_or_odd' k
  · have hn' : gI n = gI m := by
      rw [he, hj, show (p : ℤ) ^ (2 * j) * m = m * ((p : ℤ) ^ j) ^ 2 by ring]
      exact gI_sq m (pow_ne_zero j hp0)
    rw [hn', psiOdd_gI_of_not_dvd p hm, map_zero]
    symm
    rw [QuotientAddGroup.eq_zero_iff]
    exact gI_mem_Lsub hPm
  · have hn' : gI n = gI ((p : ℤ) * m) := by
      rw [he, hj, show (p : ℤ) ^ (2 * j + 1) * m = ((p : ℤ) * m) * ((p : ℤ) ^ j) ^ 2 by ring]
      exact gI_sq _ (pow_ne_zero j hp0)
    rw [hn', psiOdd_gI_prime_mul p hm, nu_gen]
    rw [nuGen_eq _ hPm rfl]

/-- Helper: $\nu\circ\psi(p)$ is the quotient map on $L(p)$ (so $\psi(p)$ is injective on $L(p)/L'(p)$). -/
theorem theta_eq {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub p) :
    (nu (p := p)) (psiOdd p x) = QuotientAddGroup.mk x := by
  refine AddSubgroup.closure_induction
    (p := fun x _ => (nu (p := p)) (psiOdd p x) = QuotientAddGroup.mk x) (fun y hy => ?_) ?_
    (fun x y _ _ hx hy => ?_) (fun x _ hx => ?_) hx
  · obtain ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact theta_gen hn
  · simp
  · rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]; rfl
  · rw [map_neg, map_neg, hx]; rfl

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 6, §11, p. 96 (key step, odd $p$).** An element of $L(p)$ in the kernel of $\psi(p)$
lies in $L'(p) = L(p-1)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, proof of Thm. 11.1 (kernel of ψ(p) on L(p), p odd), pp. 95-96"]
theorem ker_psiOdd {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub p) (h : psiOdd p x = 0) : x ∈ Lsub (p - 1) := by
  have := theta_eq hx
  rw [h, map_zero] at this
  exact (QuotientAddGroup.eq_zero_iff x).mp this.symm

/-- Helper: the prime $p$ lies in $P(p)$. -/
theorem PInt_prime_self : PInt p (p : ℤ) :=
  ⟨by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero, fun q _ hd => Nat.le_of_dvd (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos
    (Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp hd)⟩

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 6, §11, p. 96 (odd $p$).** $\psi(p)$ maps $L(p)$ onto $W(\mathbb F_p)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, proof of Thm. 11.1 (ψ(p) maps L(p) onto W(p), p odd), p. 96"]
theorem psiOdd_surj (w : W (ZMod p)) : ∃ x ∈ Lsub p, psiOdd p x = w := by
  have hp2 := p_ne_two_of_inv (p := p)
  refine W_induction (P := fun w => ∃ x ∈ Lsub p, psiOdd p x = w) ⟨0, zero_mem _, map_zero _⟩ ?_ ?_ ?_ w
  · rintro _ _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨x + y, add_mem hx hy, map_add _ _ _⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨-x, neg_mem hx, map_neg _ _⟩
  · intro α
    have hc := PInt_valMinAbs α
    refine ⟨gI ((p : ℤ) * (α : ZMod p).valMinAbs),
      gI_mem_Lsub (PInt_prime_self.mul (hc.mono (Nat.sub_le p 1))), ?_⟩
    rw [psiOdd_gI_prime_mul p (not_dvd_of_PInt hc)]
    congr 1
    exact Units.ext (ZMod.coe_valMinAbs _)

end Local

/-! ### The prime $2$ and the base case -/

theorem PInt_zero_iff_one {n : ℤ} : PInt 1 n ↔ PInt 0 n := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h0, h⟩
    exact ⟨h0, fun q hq hd => absurd (h q hq hd) (by have := hq.two_le; omega)⟩
  · exact fun h => h.mono (Nat.zero_le 1)

/-- Helper: a generator of $L(0)$ is $\pm\langle 1\rangle$. -/
theorem PInt_zero_eq {n : ℤ} (h : PInt 0 n) : n = 1 ∨ n = -1 := by
  by_contra hne
  have hne' : n.natAbs ≠ 1 := by
    intro h1
    rcases Int.natAbs_eq_iff.mp h1 with h2 | h2
    · exact hne (Or.inl (by simpa using h2))
    · exact hne (Or.inr (by simpa using h2))
  have hq := Nat.minFac_prime hne'
  have := h.2 _ hq (Int.natCast_dvd.mpr (Nat.minFac_dvd _))
  have := hq.two_le
  omega

/-- Helper: $L(0)$ is the subgroup $\mathbb Z\langle 1\rangle$. -/
theorem Lsub_zero {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub 0) : ∃ z : ℤ, x = z • gI 1 := by
  refine AddSubgroup.closure_induction (p := fun x _ => ∃ z : ℤ, x = z • gI 1) (fun y hy => ?_) ⟨0, by simp⟩
    (fun x y _ _ hx hy => ?_) (fun x _ hx => ?_) hx
  · obtain ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩ := hy
    rcases PInt_zero_eq hn with rfl | rfl
    · exact ⟨1, by simp⟩
    · exact ⟨-1, by rw [gI_neg]; simp⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact ⟨a + b, by rw [add_smul]⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨-a, by rw [neg_smul]⟩

/-- Helper: $L(2)$ consists of the elements $a\langle 1\rangle + b\langle 2\rangle$. -/
theorem Lsub_two {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub 2) : ∃ a b : ℤ, x = a • gI 1 + b • gI 2 := by
  refine AddSubgroup.closure_induction (p := fun x _ => ∃ a b : ℤ, x = a • gI 1 + b • gI 2)
    (fun y hy => ?_) ⟨0, 0, by simp⟩ (fun x y _ _ hx hy => ?_) (fun x _ hx => ?_) hx
  · obtain ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩ := hy
    have : Fact (Nat.Prime 2) := ⟨Nat.prime_two⟩
    obtain ⟨k, m, hm, he⟩ := exists_pow_mul 2 le_rfl _ n rfl hn.1
    have hPm : PInt 1 m := by
      refine ⟨fun h => hm (h ▸ dvd_zero _), fun q hq hd => ?_⟩
      have h1 : q ≤ 2 := hn.2 q hq (hd.trans ⟨((2 : ℕ) : ℤ) ^ k, by rw [he]; push_cast; ring⟩)
      rcases Nat.lt_or_ge q 2 with h | h
      · omega
      · exfalso
        have : q = 2 := by omega
        subst this
        exact hm hd
    rcases PInt_zero_eq (PInt_zero_iff_one.mp hPm) with rfl | rfl
    · obtain ⟨j, hj | hj⟩ := Nat.even_or_odd' k
      · refine ⟨1, 0, ?_⟩
        have : gI n = gI 1 := by
          rw [he, hj, show ((2 : ℕ) : ℤ) ^ (2 * j) * 1 = 1 * (2 ^ j) ^ 2 by push_cast; ring]
          exact gI_sq 1 (pow_ne_zero j (by norm_num))
        rw [this]; simp
      · refine ⟨0, 1, ?_⟩
        have : gI n = gI 2 := by
          rw [he, hj, show ((2 : ℕ) : ℤ) ^ (2 * j + 1) * 1 = 2 * (2 ^ j) ^ 2 by push_cast; ring]
          exact gI_sq 2 (pow_ne_zero j (by norm_num))
        rw [this]; simp
    · obtain ⟨j, hj | hj⟩ := Nat.even_or_odd' k
      · refine ⟨-1, 0, ?_⟩
        have : gI n = -gI 1 := by
          rw [he, hj, show ((2 : ℕ) : ℤ) ^ (2 * j) * (-1) = -(1 * (2 ^ j) ^ 2) by push_cast; ring, gI_neg]
          rw [gI_sq 1 (pow_ne_zero j (by norm_num))]
        rw [this]; simp
      · refine ⟨0, -1, ?_⟩
        have : gI n = -gI 2 := by
          rw [he, hj, show ((2 : ℕ) : ℤ) ^ (2 * j + 1) * (-1) = -(2 * (2 ^ j) ^ 2) by push_cast; ring, gI_neg]
          rw [gI_sq 2 (pow_ne_zero j (by norm_num))]
        rw [this]; simp
  · obtain ⟨a, b, rfl⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨a', b', rfl⟩ := hy
    exact ⟨a + a', b + b', by rw [add_smul, add_smul]; abel⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, b, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨-a, -b, by rw [neg_smul, neg_smul]; abel⟩

/-- Helper: $2\langle 2\rangle = 2\langle 1\rangle$ in $W(\mathbb Q)$ (Cassels, p. 94). -/
theorem two_gI_two : (2 : ℤ) • gI 2 = (2 : ℤ) • gI 1 := by
  have key := gI_add (n := 2) (m := 2) (by norm_num) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)
  have e1 : gI (2 + 2) = gI 1 := by
    have := gI_sq 1 (m := 2) (by norm_num)
    simpa using this
  have e2 : gI (2 * 2 * (2 + 2)) = gI 1 := by
    have := gI_sq 1 (m := 4) (by norm_num)
    simpa using this
  rw [e1, e2] at key
  rw [two_smul, two_smul]
  exact key

/-- Helper: $\psi(2)\langle 1\rangle = 0$. -/
theorem psiTwo_gI_one : psiTwo (gI 1) = 0 := by
  rw [psiTwo_gI (by norm_num)]; simp [padicValInt]

/-- Helper: $\psi(2)\langle 2\rangle = 1$. -/
theorem psiTwo_gI_two : psiTwo (gI 2) = 1 := by
  rw [psiTwo_gI (by norm_num)]
  have : Fact (Nat.Prime 2) := ⟨Nat.prime_two⟩
  simp [padicValInt]

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 6, §11, p. 94 (the case $p = 2$).** An element of $L(2)$ in the kernel of $\psi(2)$ lies in
$L'(2) = L(1)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, proof of Thm. 11.1 (the case p = 2), p. 94"]
theorem ker_psiTwo {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub 2) (h : psiTwo x = 0) : x ∈ Lsub 1 := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, rfl⟩ := Lsub_two hx
  rw [map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul, psiTwo_gI_one, psiTwo_gI_two] at h
  simp only [smul_zero, zero_add, zsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := (ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd b 2).mp h
  rw [show ((2 : ℕ) : ℤ) * c = c * 2 by push_cast; ring, mul_smul, two_gI_two, ← mul_smul, ← add_smul]
  exact zsmul_mem (gI_mem_Lsub (PInt.one 1)) _

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 6, §11, p. 94 (the case $p = 2$).** $\psi(2)$ maps $L(2)$ onto $\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, proof of Thm. 11.1 (the case p = 2), p. 94"]
theorem psiTwo_surj (w : ZMod 2) : ∃ x ∈ Lsub 2, psiTwo x = w := by
  have hw : w = 0 ∨ w = 1 := by revert w; decide
  rcases hw with rfl | rfl
  · exact ⟨0, zero_mem _, map_zero _⟩
  · refine ⟨gI 2, gI_mem_Lsub ⟨by norm_num, fun q hq hd => ?_⟩, psiTwo_gI_two⟩
    exact Nat.le_of_dvd (by norm_num) (Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp hd)

/-! ### The odd primes as an index type, and the combined map -/

/-- The odd primes (the index type of the odd part of the direct sum). -/
abbrev OddPrime : Type := {p : ℕ // p.Prime ∧ p ≠ 2}

/-- Helper: an odd prime is a prime (for field instances on $\mathbb Z/p$). -/
instance (p : OddPrime) : Fact p.1.Prime := ⟨p.2.1⟩

/-- Helper: $2$ is invertible modulo an odd prime. -/
instance oddInv (p : OddPrime) : Invertible (2 : ZMod p.1) := invertibleOfNonzero (by
  intro h
  have := (ZMod.natCast_eq_zero_iff 2 p.1).mp (by exact_mod_cast h)
  have := (Nat.prime_dvd_prime_iff_eq p.2.1 Nat.prime_two).mp this
  exact p.2.2 this)

/-- The summand $W(p) = W(\mathbb F_p)$ for an odd prime $p$ (Cassels (11.1)). -/
abbrev Wp (p : OddPrime) : Type := W (ZMod p.1)

/-- $\psi(p) : W(\mathbb Q) \to W(p)$ for an odd prime $p$, as a function of the index `p : OddPrime` (`psiOdd` with the
instance "$2$ is invertible modulo $p$" supplied by `oddInv`). -/
def psiOddAt (p : OddPrime) : W ℚ →+ Wp p := @psiOdd p.1 _ (oddInv p)

open Classical in
/-- Helper: a finite set of odd primes outside which $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle = 0$. -/
def suppSet (a : ℚˣ) : Finset OddPrime :=
  (Nat.primeFactors ((a : ℚ).num.natAbs * (a : ℚ).den)).subtype (fun p => p.Prime ∧ p ≠ 2)

/-- Helper: $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle = 0$ unless $p$ divides the numerator or denominator of $a$. -/
theorem psiOddAt_gW_of_not_mem (a : ℚˣ) (q : OddPrime) (h : q ∉ suppSet a) : psiOddAt q (gW a) = 0 := by
  classical
  have hmem : ¬ q.1 ∈ Nat.primeFactors ((a : ℚ).num.natAbs * (a : ℚ).den) := by
    simpa [suppSet] using h
  have hN : (a : ℚ).num.natAbs * (a : ℚ).den ≠ 0 :=
    mul_ne_zero (Int.natAbs_ne_zero.mpr (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr a.ne_zero)) (a : ℚ).den_nz
  have hnd : ¬ q.1 ∣ (a : ℚ).num.natAbs * (a : ℚ).den := fun hd =>
    hmem (Nat.mem_primeFactors.mpr ⟨q.2.1, hd, hN⟩)
  have h1 : ¬ q.1 ∣ (a : ℚ).num.natAbs := fun hd => hnd (hd.mul_right _)
  have h2 : ¬ q.1 ∣ (a : ℚ).den := fun hd => hnd (hd.mul_left _)
  have h1' : ¬ (q.1 : ℤ) ∣ (a : ℚ).num := fun hd => h1 (Int.natCast_dvd.mp hd)
  unfold psiOddAt
  apply @psiOdd_gen_of_even q.1 _ (oddInv q)
  have : padicValRat q.1 (a : ℚ) = 0 := by
    simp only [padicValRat, padicValInt.eq_zero_of_not_dvd h1', padicValNat.eq_zero_of_not_dvd h2]
    simp
  rw [this]
  exact ⟨0, by simp⟩

open Classical in
/-- Helper: the generator values of the odd part of the combined map, as finitely supported families. -/
def gDS (a : ℚˣ) : Π₀ q : OddPrime, Wp q := DFinsupp.mk (suppSet a) (fun q => psiOddAt q (gW a))

/-- Helper: the $p$-th component of `gDS a` is $\psi(p)\langle a\rangle$. -/
theorem gDS_apply (a : ℚˣ) (q : OddPrime) : gDS a q = psiOddAt q (gW a) := by
  classical
  unfold gDS
  rw [DFinsupp.mk_apply]
  by_cases h : q ∈ suppSet a
  · simp [h]
  · simp [h, psiOddAt_gW_of_not_mem a q h]

/-- Helper: relation (i) for `gDS`. -/
theorem gDS_rel1 (a b : ℚˣ) : gDS (a * b ^ 2) = gDS a := by
  ext q
  rw [gDS_apply, gDS_apply, gW_sq]

/-- Helper: relation (ii) for `gDS`. -/
theorem gDS_rel2 (a b : ℚˣ) (hab : (a : ℚ) + b ≠ 0) :
    gDS a + gDS b = gDS (Units.mk0 _ hab) + gDS (a * b * Units.mk0 _ hab) := by
  ext q
  simp only [DFinsupp.add_apply, gDS_apply]
  rw [← map_add, ← map_add, gW_add a b hab]

/-- Helper: relation (iii) for `gDS`. -/
theorem gDS_rel3 : gDS 1 + gDS (-1) = 0 := by
  ext q
  simp only [DFinsupp.add_apply, gDS_apply, DFinsupp.zero_apply]
  rw [← map_add, gW_add_neg, map_zero]

/-- Helper: $(\psi(p))_{p \text{ odd}} : W(\mathbb Q) \to \bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(\mathbb F_p)$. -/
def PhiOdd : W ℚ →+ Π₀ q : OddPrime, Wp q :=
  (W_lift (K := ℚ) gDS gDS_rel1 gDS_rel2 gDS_rel3).exists.choose

/-- Helper: `PhiOdd` sends $\langle a\rangle$ to `gDS a`. -/
theorem PhiOdd_gen (a : ℚˣ) : PhiOdd (gW a) = gDS a :=
  (W_lift (K := ℚ) gDS gDS_rel1 gDS_rel2 gDS_rel3).exists.choose_spec a

/-- Helper: the $p$-th component of `PhiOdd x` is $\psi(p)x$. -/
theorem PhiOdd_apply (x : W ℚ) (q : OddPrime) : PhiOdd x q = psiOddAt q x := by
  have : (DFinsupp.evalAddMonoidHom (β := fun q : OddPrime => Wp q) q).comp PhiOdd = psiOddAt q :=
    W_hom_ext _ _ fun a => by
      show (PhiOdd (gW a)) q = psiOddAt q (gW a)
      rw [PhiOdd_gen, gDS_apply]
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun this x

/-- **The combined map of Theorem 11.1**, $\Phi : W(\mathbb Q) \to W(\infty) \oplus W(2) \oplus \bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(p)
= \mathbb Z \times \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z \times \bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(\mathbb F_p)$,
$x \mapsto (\psi(\infty)x, \psi(2)x, (\psi(p)x)_{p \text{ odd}})$. -/
def Phi : W ℚ →+ ℤ × ZMod 2 × Π₀ q : OddPrime, Wp q := psiInf.prod (psiTwo.prod PhiOdd)

/-- Helper: the components of `Phi`. -/
theorem Phi_apply (x : W ℚ) : Phi x = (psiInf x, psiTwo x, PhiOdd x) := rfl

/-! ### The induction over the filtration -/

/-- Helper: the tuples whose components at all primes larger than $N$ vanish. -/
def SuppSub (N : ℕ) : AddSubgroup (ℤ × ZMod 2 × Π₀ q : OddPrime, Wp q) where
  carrier := {t | (N < 2 → t.2.1 = 0) ∧ ∀ q : OddPrime, N < q.1 → t.2.2 q = 0}
  zero_mem' := ⟨fun _ => rfl, fun _ _ => rfl⟩
  add_mem' := by
    rintro a b ⟨ha1, ha2⟩ ⟨hb1, hb2⟩
    exact ⟨fun h => by simp [ha1 h, hb1 h], fun q h => by simp [ha2 q h, hb2 q h]⟩
  neg_mem' := by
    rintro a ⟨ha1, ha2⟩
    exact ⟨fun h => by simp [ha1 h], fun q h => by simp [ha2 q h]⟩

/-- Helper: membership in `SuppSub N`. -/
theorem mem_SuppSub {N : ℕ} {t : ℤ × ZMod 2 × Π₀ q : OddPrime, Wp q} :
    t ∈ SuppSub N ↔ (N < 2 → t.2.1 = 0) ∧ ∀ q : OddPrime, N < q.1 → t.2.2 q = 0 := Iff.rfl

/-- Helper: `Phi` maps $L(N)$ into the tuples supported at the places $\le N$. -/
theorem Phi_mem {N : ℕ} {x : W ℚ} (hx : x ∈ Lsub N) : Phi x ∈ SuppSub N := by
  have : Lsub N ≤ (SuppSub N).comap Phi := by
    refine AddSubgroup.closure_le _ |>.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨fun hN => ?_, fun q hq => ?_⟩
    · show psiTwo (gI n) = 0
      rw [psiTwo_gI hn.1]
      have hn2 : ¬ (2 : ℤ) ∣ n := fun hd => by
        have := hn.2 2 Nat.prime_two (by exact_mod_cast hd)
        omega
      have h0 : padicValInt 2 n = 0 := padicValInt.eq_zero_of_not_dvd hn2
      rw [h0]; simp
    · show PhiOdd (gI n) q = 0
      rw [PhiOdd_apply]
      refine @psiOdd_gI_of_not_dvd q.1 _ (oddInv q) n (fun hd => ?_)
      have := hn.2 q.1 q.2.1 hd
      omega
  exact this hx

/-- Helper: $\Phi\langle 1\rangle = (1, 0, 0)$. -/
theorem Phi_gI_one : Phi (gI 1) = (1, 0, 0) := by
  have h3 : PhiOdd (gI 1) = 0 := by
    ext q
    rw [PhiOdd_apply]
    refine @psiOdd_gI_of_not_dvd q.1 _ (oddInv q) 1 (fun hd => q.2.1.not_dvd_one ?_)
    exact Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp (by simpa using hd)
  rw [Phi_apply, psiInf_gI one_ne_zero, psiTwo_gI_one, h3]
  simp

/-- Helper: if $N+1$ is not prime then $P(N+1) = P(N)$. -/
theorem lsub_succ_of_not_prime {N : ℕ} (h : ¬ (N + 1).Prime) {n : ℤ} (hn : PInt (N + 1) n) : PInt N n :=
  ⟨hn.1, fun q hq hd => by
    have := hn.2 q hq hd
    rcases Nat.lt_or_ge q (N + 1) with h1 | h1
    · omega
    · exfalso
      have : q = N + 1 := by omega
      subst this
      exact h hq⟩

/-- Helper (the induction of Cassels' proof, p. 94): for every $N$, $\Phi$ maps $L(N)$ bijectively onto the tuples supported at the places $\le N$. -/
theorem main_ind : ∀ N : ℕ, (∀ x ∈ Lsub N, Phi x = 0 → x = 0) ∧
    (∀ t ∈ SuppSub N, ∃ x ∈ Lsub N, Phi x = t) := by
  intro N
  induction N with
  | zero =>
    constructor
    · intro x hx h
      obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Lsub_zero hx
      rw [map_zsmul, Phi_gI_one] at h
      have := congrArg Prod.fst h
      simp at this
      simp [this]
    · intro t ht
      obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := ht
      refine ⟨t.1 • gI 1, zsmul_mem (gI_mem_Lsub (PInt.one 0)) _, ?_⟩
      rw [map_zsmul, Phi_gI_one]
      have e1 : t.2.1 = 0 := h1 (by norm_num)
      have e2 : t.2.2 = 0 := by
        ext q
        exact h2 q (by have := q.2.1.pos; omega)
      ext <;> simp [e1, e2]
  | succ N ih =>
    by_cases hM : (N + 1).Prime
    · by_cases h2 : N + 1 = 2
      · obtain rfl : N = 1 := by omega
        constructor
        · intro x hx h
          apply ih.1 x _ h
          refine ker_psiTwo hx ?_
          have := congrArg (fun t => t.2.1) h
          simpa [Phi_apply] using this
        · intro t ht
          obtain ⟨y, hy, hyv⟩ := psiTwo_surj t.2.1
          have ht' : t - Phi y ∈ SuppSub 2 := sub_mem ht (Phi_mem hy)
          obtain ⟨x, hx, hxv⟩ := ih.2 (t - Phi y) (by
            refine ⟨fun _ => ?_, fun q hq => ?_⟩
            · simp [Phi_apply, hyv]
            · refine ht'.2 q ?_
              have := q.2.1.two_le
              have := q.2.2
              omega)
          exact ⟨x + y, add_mem (Lsub_mono (by norm_num) hx) hy, by rw [map_add, hxv]; abel⟩
      · obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ : ∃ P : OddPrime, P.1 = N + 1 := ⟨⟨N + 1, hM, h2⟩, rfl⟩
        have hker : ∀ x ∈ Lsub (N + 1), psiOddAt P x = 0 → x ∈ Lsub N := fun x hx h => by
          have := @ker_psiOdd P.1 _ (oddInv P) x (hP ▸ hx) h
          rwa [hP, Nat.add_sub_cancel] at this
        have hsurj : ∀ w : Wp P, ∃ x ∈ Lsub (N + 1), psiOddAt P x = w := fun w => by
          obtain ⟨x, hx, hxw⟩ := @psiOdd_surj P.1 _ (oddInv P) w
          exact ⟨x, hP ▸ hx, hxw⟩
        constructor
        · intro x hx h
          apply ih.1 x _ h
          have h0 : psiOddAt P x = 0 := by
            have := congrArg (fun t => t.2.2 P) h
            simpa [Phi_apply, PhiOdd_apply] using this
          exact hker x hx h0
        · intro t ht
          obtain ⟨y, hy, hyv⟩ := hsurj (t.2.2 P)
          have ht' : t - Phi y ∈ SuppSub (N + 1) := sub_mem ht (Phi_mem hy)
          obtain ⟨x, hx, hxv⟩ := ih.2 (t - Phi y) (by
            refine ⟨fun hlt => ?_, fun q hq => ?_⟩
            · exfalso
              have := hM.two_le
              omega
            · rcases Nat.lt_or_ge (N + 1) q.1 with h1 | h1
              · exact ht'.2 q h1
              · have hq1 : q = P := Subtype.ext (by omega)
                subst hq1
                simp [Phi_apply, PhiOdd_apply, hyv])
          exact ⟨x + y, add_mem (Lsub_mono (by omega) hx) hy, by rw [map_add, hxv]; abel⟩
    · have hle : Lsub (N + 1) ≤ Lsub N := by
        refine AddSubgroup.closure_le _ |>.mpr ?_
        rintro _ ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
        exact gI_mem_Lsub (lsub_succ_of_not_prime hM hn)
      constructor
      · intro x hx h
        exact ih.1 x (hle hx) h
      · intro t ht
        obtain ⟨x, hx, hxv⟩ := ih.2 t (by
          refine ⟨fun hlt => ?_, fun q hq => ?_⟩
          · apply ht.1
            rcases Nat.lt_or_ge N 1 with h0 | h0
            · omega
            · exfalso
              have : N = 1 := by omega
              subst this
              exact hM Nat.prime_two
          · refine ht.2 q ?_
            rcases Nat.lt_or_ge (N + 1) q.1 with h1 | h1
            · exact h1
            · exfalso
              have : q.1 = N + 1 := by omega
              exact hM (this ▸ q.2.1))
        exact ⟨x, Lsub_mono (Nat.le_succ N) hx, hxv⟩

/-- Helper: $\langle a\rangle = \langle ND\rangle$ for $a = N/D$ in lowest terms. -/
theorem gW_eq_gI (a : ℚˣ) : gW a = gI ((a : ℚ).num * (a : ℚ).den) := by
  have hn : (a : ℚ).num * ((a : ℚ).den : ℤ) ≠ 0 :=
    mul_ne_zero (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr a.ne_zero) (by exact_mod_cast (a : ℚ).den_nz)
  have hd : ((a : ℚ).den : ℚ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (a : ℚ).den_nz
  rw [gI_eq hn, ← gW_sq a (Units.mk0 (((a : ℚ).den : ℤ) : ℚ) (by exact_mod_cast hd))]
  congr 1
  refine Units.ext ?_
  have := Rat.mul_den_eq_num (a : ℚ)
  simp only [Units.val_mul, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, Units.val_mk0]
  push_cast
  rw [pow_two, ← mul_assoc, this]

/-- Helper: every element of $W(\mathbb Q)$ lies in some $L(N)$ (the union of the $L(N)$ is $W(\mathbb Q)$). -/
theorem exists_Lsub (x : W ℚ) : ∃ N : ℕ, x ∈ Lsub N := by
  refine W_induction (P := fun x => ∃ N : ℕ, x ∈ Lsub N) ⟨0, zero_mem _⟩ ?_ ?_ ?_ x
  · rintro _ _ ⟨N, hN⟩ ⟨M, hM⟩
    exact ⟨max N M, add_mem (Lsub_mono (le_max_left _ _) hN) (Lsub_mono (le_max_right _ _) hM)⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨N, hN⟩
    exact ⟨N, neg_mem hN⟩
  · intro a
    rw [gW_eq_gI]
    have hn : (a : ℚ).num * ((a : ℚ).den : ℤ) ≠ 0 :=
      mul_ne_zero (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr a.ne_zero) (by exact_mod_cast (a : ℚ).den_nz)
    exact ⟨_, gI_mem_Lsub (PInt.of_natAbs_le hn le_rfl)⟩

/-- The combined map $\Phi$ is injective (Cassels, Theorem 11.1). -/
theorem Phi_injective : Function.Injective Phi := by
  rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_Lsub x
  exact (main_ind N).1 x hN hx

/-- The combined map $\Phi$ is surjective (Cassels, Theorem 11.1). -/
theorem Phi_surjective : Function.Surjective Phi := by
  classical
  intro t
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ : ∃ N, t ∈ SuppSub N := by
    refine ⟨t.2.2.support.sup (fun q => q.1) + 2, fun h => by omega, fun q hq => ?_⟩
    by_contra h0
    have hmem : q ∈ t.2.2.support := DFinsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr h0
    have := Finset.le_sup (f := fun q : OddPrime => q.1) hmem
    omega
  obtain ⟨x, -, hx⟩ := (main_ind N).2 t hN
  exact ⟨x, hx⟩

/-! ### The values of the maps $\psi(p)$, and Theorem 11.1 -/

/-- **Cassels (11.3)-(11.4), p. 93.** For an odd prime $p$, an integer $m$ prime to $p$ and $l \ge 0$ (so
$p^{l}m = p^{l}u$ with $u = m$ a $p$-adic unit of residue $\bar m$): $\psi(p)\langle p^{l}m\rangle = \langle\bar m\rangle$
if $l$ is odd and $0$ if $l$ is even. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, (11.3)-(11.4), p. 93"]
theorem psiOddAt_pow_mul (p : OddPrime) (m : ℤ) (hm : ¬ (p.1 : ℤ) ∣ m) (l : ℕ) :
    psiOddAt p (gI ((p.1 : ℤ) ^ l * m)) =
      if Even l then 0 else gW (Units.mk0 (m : ZMod p.1) (fun h => hm ((ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd m p.1).mp h))) := by
  have hm0 : m ≠ 0 := fun h => hm (h ▸ dvd_zero _)
  have hn : (p.1 : ℤ) ^ l * m ≠ 0 :=
    mul_ne_zero (pow_ne_zero _ (by exact_mod_cast p.2.1.ne_zero)) hm0
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := @val_rc_int p.1 _ (oddInv p) m hm l hn
  unfold psiOddAt
  rw [gI_eq hn, @psiOdd_gen p.1 _ (oddInv p), h1]
  by_cases he : Even l
  · simp [he]
  · simp only [Int.even_coe_nat, he, if_false]
    congr 1
    exact Units.ext h2

/-- **Cassels (11.6)-(11.7), p. 93** ((11.7) is $\lvert a\rvert_2 = 2^{-l}$ on the page image). $\psi(2)\langle a\rangle$ is the $2$-adic valuation
$l = v_2(a)$ of $a \in \mathbb Q^{\times}$ modulo $2$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, (11.6)-(11.7), p. 93"]
theorem psiTwo_gW (a : ℚˣ) : psiTwo (gW a) = ((padicValRat 2 (a : ℚ) : ℤ) : ZMod 2) := by
  have h : val 2 (castU 2 a) = padicValRat 2 (a : ℚ) := by simp [val, castU]
  rw [psiTwo_gen, h]

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 6, Theorem 11.1 (p. 94).** *The maps $\psi(p)$ (including $p = \infty$) establish an isomorphism
between $W(\mathbb Q)$ and the direct sum of the $W(p)$.* Here the direct sum is $W(\infty) \oplus W(2) \oplus
\bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(p) = \mathbb Z \times \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z \times \bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(\mathbb F_p)$, and the
statement is that the combined map `Phi` $= (\psi(\infty), \psi(2), (\psi(p))_{p \text{ odd}})$ is bijective
(unconditional; no input is assumed). -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, Thm. 11.1, p. 94"]
theorem witt_rationals_bijective : Function.Bijective Phi := ⟨Phi_injective, Phi_surjective⟩

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 6, Theorem 11.1 (p. 94), as an isomorphism of groups:**
$W(\mathbb Q) \cong \mathbb Z \times \mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z \times \bigoplus_{p \text{ odd}} W(\mathbb F_p)$, with
$\langle a\rangle \mapsto (\operatorname{sign}(a), v_2(a) \bmod 2, (\psi(p)\langle a\rangle)_{p \text{ odd}})$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 6, §11, Thm. 11.1, p. 94 (as an isomorphism)"]
def wittRationalsEquiv : W ℚ ≃+ ℤ × ZMod 2 × Π₀ p : OddPrime, Wp p :=
  AddEquiv.ofBijective Phi witt_rationals_bijective

/-- The isomorphism of Theorem 11.1 is given componentwise by $\psi(\infty)$, $\psi(2)$ and the $\psi(p)$, $p$ odd. -/
theorem wittRationalsEquiv_apply (x : W ℚ) :
    wittRationalsEquiv x = (psiInf x, psiTwo x, PhiOdd x) := rfl

/-- The odd components of the isomorphism of Theorem 11.1 are the maps $\psi(p)$. -/
theorem wittRationalsEquiv_odd (x : W ℚ) (p : OddPrime) : (wittRationalsEquiv x).2.2 p = psiOddAt p x :=
  PhiOdd_apply x p

end QuadFormsKB.Cassels.Ch6

